tasks.title:
Expose window.bootstrap + add a jQuery modal compat shim in resources/js/app.js (Laravel app, this repo root: G:\ipma_erp2). Bug (fully diagnosed): the bundle loads bootstrap 5.3.8 via `require('bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle')` but webpack takes the UMD module.exports branch, so `window.bootstrap` is NEVER set at runtime; Bootstrap 5 ships no jQuery plugin, so `$.fn.modal` does not exist either. Result: every `new bootstrap.Modal(el)` (the four resources/js/modules/leaveapproval*/index.js approve-button handlers) throws ReferenceError: bootstrap is not defined, and every legacy `$('#x').modal('show'|'hide')` call (resources/js/modules/appraisalform/form.js x16, appraisalapoint/index.js x2, appraisalmark/form.js x1, plus the four leaveapproval modules' `.modal('hide')` on submit) throws TypeError - modals never open/close. Fix in ONE file, resources/js/app.js: inside the existing `try { ... } catch (e) {}` block, immediately after the existing line `	window.config = require('./config/plugins').default;` add EXACTLY these lines (tabs for indentation to match the file):

	// expose Bootstrap 5 as a global (webpack keeps the UMD module-scoped otherwise)
	window.bootstrap = require('bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle');

	// jQuery modal compat shim - Bootstrap 5 ships no jQuery plugin, but pages
	// still call $(el).modal('show' | 'hide')
	$.fn.modal = function (action) {
		return this.each(function () {
			var instance = window.bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(this);
			if (typeof action === 'string' && instance[action]) {
				instance[action]();
			}
		});
	};

Do NOT change any other line (the requires above, the catch, the axios section below). Verify: run `npx mix` - it must compile successfully; then `grep -c 'window.bootstrap =' public/js/app.js` must print >= 1 and `grep -c 'fn.modal = function' public/js/app.js` must print >= 1 (the shim survived minification). Report the mix result and both grep counts.

